I go to a nearby vegetable vendor's cart.
There I look at my list.
I say to the vendor, "Brother, first give me a quarter kilo of onions."
"Then give me fresh green chilies."
He weighs the onions and green chilies.
He puts those items in a bag.
After that I say, "Please give me one lemon."
He asks, "Madam, is anything else needed?"
I say, "Yes, I also need green coriander."
He asks again, "How much coriander?"
I say, "Give me one large bunch."
He puts the lemon and the coriander in the bag.
I mentally count the remaining items on my list.
Now everything is ready for making Kande Pohe.
I ask the vegetable vendor the price.
He says, "Fifty rupees."
I give him the money.
Then I take the bag and walk towards home.
